# Replace the gains the STM32 writes to the ODrives.
#
# Between runs only: the board REFUSES a change while it is driving, because a
# velocity gain changing under load is a step change in torque with a leg's
# weight behind it. Stand down first (/zeus/stand_down).
#
# The board re-sends these to every drive on each arm, so a drive that reboots
# comes back with the gains being tuned rather than its own saved ones. They
# are NOT written to the drives' non-volatile memory: power-cycle the board and
# it goes back to the table in its robot_config.c. When a value is settled, put
# it there.
#
# Joint order is the J_* order in NexusState.msg. A NEGATIVE value means "leave
# that drive's own saved value alone".
#
# Units are the ODrive's own:
#   pos_gain              (turn/s) per turn of error
#   vel_gain              Nm per (turn/s) of error
#   vel_integrator_gain   Nm per turn of accumulated error

float32[8] pos_gain
float32[8] vel_gain
float32[8] vel_integrator_gain
---
bool applied            # false = the board refused them, see message
string message
